# SmartSave.io — Full Production Fix

The backend keeps failing with "yt-dlp binary missing" because of multiple interconnected issues: wrong binary paths, mixed frontend/backend concerns, incorrect Dockerfile configuration, and deployment misconfigs. This plan fixes everything in one shot.

## What's Wrong (Root Cause Analysis)

| # | Issue | Impact |
|---|-------|--------|
| 1 | `bin/` contains 216MB of Windows [.exe](file:///d:/Webdownload/bin/ffmpeg.exe) binaries ([yt-dlp.exe](file:///d:/Webdownload/bin/yt-dlp.exe), [ffmpeg.exe](file:///d:/Webdownload/bin/ffmpeg.exe), [ffprobe.exe](file:///d:/Webdownload/bin/ffprobe.exe)) | Won't work on Linux servers |
| 2 | [package.json](file:///d:/Webdownload/package.json) mixes frontend (vite) and backend (express) — Render installs vite as devDependency and `npm install --production` skips it, but the `start` script tries both | Build confusion |
| 3 | `EXPOSE 3001` in Dockerfile but Render assigns `PORT` via env var (usually 10000) | Port mismatch warnings |
| 4 | Startup log prints `'Global Path'` instead of actual `YT_DLP_PATH` value | Misleading diagnostics |
| 5 | CORS only allows `*.vercel.app` regex — won't match custom domains | API blocked for custom domains |
| 6 | No `.dockerignore` — Docker copies `node_modules/`, `bin/`, `src/`, `dist/` into image (wasted 300MB+) | Slow builds, bloated image |
| 7 | Render free tier spins down → cold starts take 30-50s → frontend times out | "Failed to fetch" on first request |
| 8 | Frontend [download.js](file:///d:/Webdownload/src/pages/download.js) hardcodes backend URL — no env-based config | Fragile deployment |

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Core

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///d:/Webdownload/server.js)
- Remove all Windows-specific logic (`isLinux` flag, [.exe](file:///d:/Webdownload/bin/ffmpeg.exe) paths)
- Hardcode Linux paths: `YT_DLP_PATH = '/usr/local/bin/yt-dlp'`, `FFMPEG_DIR = '/usr/bin'`
- Keep Windows fallback for local dev only (check `os.platform()`)
- Fix startup log to print actual binary path, not `'Global Path'`
- Add `ffmpeg` existence check alongside `yt-dlp`
- Expand CORS to include the user's specific Vercel domain + custom domains
- Add request timeout handling for cold starts

#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile](file:///d:/Webdownload/Dockerfile)
- Remove hardcoded `EXPOSE 3001` (Render uses `$PORT`)
- Add `EXPOSE $PORT` or remove EXPOSE entirely (Render ignores it anyway)
- Verify `yt-dlp` AND `ffmpeg` during build with version checks

#### [NEW] [.dockerignore](file:///d:/Webdownload/.dockerignore)
- Exclude `node_modules/`, `bin/`, `src/`, `dist/`, `public/`, [index.html](file:///d:/Webdownload/index.html), [vercel.json](file:///d:/Webdownload/vercel.json), `.git/`
- Only copy `package*.json` and [server.js](file:///d:/Webdownload/server.js) into the Docker image

#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///d:/Webdownload/package.json)
- Keep as-is since Dockerfile only copies [server.js](file:///d:/Webdownload/server.js) — vite deps won't be installed with `--production`

---

### Frontend Integration

#### [MODIFY] [download.js](file:///d:/Webdownload/src/pages/download.js)
- Increase fetch timeout to 60s to handle Render cold starts
- Add retry logic (1 retry after 5s) for "Failed to fetch" errors
- Keep current `API_BASE` detection (already points to `smartsaver-downloader`)

---

### Deployment Config

#### [MODIFY] [.gitignore](file:///d:/Webdownload/.gitignore)
- Already excludes `bin/` — confirmed correct
- Add `*.exe` as extra safety

## Target Folder Structure (What Gets Deployed)

```
Render (Backend Docker):         Vercel (Frontend):
├── /app/                        ├── index.html
│   ├── server.js                ├── public/
│   ├── package.json             │   └── favicon.svg
│   └── node_modules/            ├── src/
│       ├── express/             │   ├── main.js
│       └── cors/                │   ├── router.js
│                                │   ├── style.css
│  System binaries:              │   ├── pages/
│  /usr/local/bin/yt-dlp         │   │   ├── download.js
│  /usr/bin/ffmpeg               │   │   ├── home.js
│  /usr/bin/ffprobe              │   │   ├── about.js
│                                │   │   ├── contact.js
│                                │   │   └── privacy.js
│                                │   └── components/
│                                │       ├── navbar.js
│                                │       └── footer.js
│                                └── vercel.json
```

## Verification Plan

### Automated (Browser Test)
1. Hit `https://smartsaver-downloader.onrender.com/api/health` — expect `{"status":"ok","ytDlpReady":true,"ffmpegReady":true}`
2. Hit the Vercel frontend, paste a YouTube URL, verify it fetches info successfully

### Manual (User Must Do)
1. Upload updated [server.js](file:///d:/Webdownload/server.js), [Dockerfile](file:///d:/Webdownload/Dockerfile), and new `.dockerignore` to GitHub
2. Trigger manual deploy on Render
3. Check Render build logs for: `yt-dlp --version` output and `ffmpeg -version` output
4. Check Render deploy logs for: `✅ yt-dlp found at /usr/local/bin/yt-dlp` and `✅ ffmpeg found at /usr/bin/ffmpeg`
5. Visit `https://smartsave-downloader.vercel.app` and test downloading a YouTube video
